What runs on one spark.

  rank_daemon.c   the process that owns a pipeline rank: hosts the stage module,
                  connects the ring, serves work
  residentd.c     holds model weights resident in GPU memory across processes, so
                  a restarting rank does not re-read a terabyte
  rank_runtime.c  per-rank runtime state
  memlink_tool.c  shared-memory link inspection

These were in tools/ because they have a main(), and then briefly in ring/
because they talk to it. Neither is what they are: ring/ is HOW NODES TALK and
node/ is WHAT RUNS ON ONE. A rank daemon uses the transport the way it uses
CUDA - as a thing it needs, not a thing it is.
